			"notes": "### Added\n\n- Support for Minecraft 1.21.2 through 26.2. 3.0.1 ran on 1.21.1 only.\n- A Continuity page in Sodium's video settings, on 1.21.1, 1.21.11, 26.1 and 26.2. It shares its options with the mod's own config screen, so changing one changes the other.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- CTM rules using a `biomes=` clause now match under Sodium. The biome lookup previously came back empty outside vanilla chunk rendering, so those rules silently never applied.\n\n### Changed\n\n- The in-game name is now Continuity: NeoForged.\n- Custom block layers are gone on 26.1 and newer. The game bakes the render layer onto each quad there, so the hook the feature relies on no longer exists. Connected and emissive textures are unaffected. This matches upstream."
		}
